['You (Candidate)', q{Interesting — three product owners all mention <strong>"mobile app 7.0"</strong>. That must be the current programme. <em>Jot that down;</em> asking about it shows I read the room before arriving.}, q{有意思——三位产品负责人都提到 <strong>"mobile app 7.0"</strong>。这应该就是当前的大项目。<em>记下来；</em>面试时问起它，说明我到场前做足了功课。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Layer three: the pain.</strong> Search the app store reviews for their mobile app — <em>the one-star reviews are the backlog</em>. Login flow complaints, session timeouts… that is what a PO in that team probably wrestles with daily.}, q{<strong>第三层：痛点。</strong>去应用商店搜他们 App 的评论——<em>一星评论就是待办清单</em>。登录流程差评、会话超时……这些大概率就是那个团队的 PO 每天在搏斗的东西。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Layer four: the JD, read backwards.</strong> Under each responsibility I ask: <em>what problem makes this responsibility exist?</em> "Own the roadmap for login journeys" ← that exists because login is where customers leak. <strong>Now I know what the first month would really be about.</strong>}, q{<strong>第四层：倒着读 JD。</strong>对每条职责问：<em>什么问题让这条职责存在？</em>"负责登录旅程路线图" ← 它存在是因为登录是客户流失点。<strong>现在我知道入职第一个月真正要做什么了。</strong>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{Last thing — <strong>my three questions for them</strong>, built from this research. One about the programme, one about the team, one about success. <em>Questions made of research are worth ten generic ones.</em>}, q{最后一件事——基于调研准备<strong>三个反问</strong>。一个关于项目、一个关于团队、一个关于成功标准。<em>由调研构成的十个问题抵得上一个泛泛之问。</em>}],
