num => 4, slug => 'star-story-bank', module => 1, read => 9, diff => '🟡 Intermediate',
title => 'Building Your STAR Story Bank', cn => '搭建你的 STAR 故事库',
focus => 'Prepare 6 stories that answer 60 questions: Situation, Task, Action, Result',
scenario => [
q{Interview preparation night two. You have listed the behavioural questions from the job ad\'s likely themes: <em>conflict, failure, leadership, pressure, ambiguity, influence</em>. Your coach\'s advice was blunt: <strong>"Do not prepare 20 answers. Prepare 6 stories, told in STAR, and map them to every question they can become."</strong>},
q{面试准备第二晚。你列出了这个岗位可能出现的行为面试题主题：<em>冲突、失败、领导力、压力、模糊性、影响力</em>。教练的建议很直接：<strong>"不要准备 20 个回答。准备 6 个 STAR 故事，然后把它们映射到所有可能的问题上。"</strong>},
q{STAR is <strong>Situation</strong> (one sentence of context), <strong>Task</strong> (what you specifically had to achieve), <strong>Action</strong> (what you did — 70% of your airtime), <strong>Result</strong> (what changed, with a number if possible). Six stories, each flexing to three or four questions, covers almost any behavioural round.},
q{STAR 即<strong>情境</strong>（一句话背景）、<strong>任务</strong>（你具体要达成什么）、<strong>行动</strong>（你做了什么——占 70% 篇幅）、<strong>结果</strong>（什么改变了，最好带数字）。6 个故事，每个可以弹性对应 3-4 个问题，几乎能覆盖任何行为面试。},
],
dialogue => [
['You (Candidate)', q{Story bank, night two. <strong>Rule one: six stories, not twenty.</strong> My six: the production incident, the stakeholder who said no, the deadline I saved, the junior I coached, the requirement I killed, the process I improved.}, q{故事库，第二晚。<strong>规则一：6 个故事，不是 20 个。</strong>我的六个：生产事故、说"不"的利益相关方、救回来的截止期、我带过的新人、我砍掉的需求、我改进的流程。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Rule two: write the Result first.</strong> If a story has no result, it is not a story, it is a memory. Each Result needs a number or a named consequence: <em>"incident cut from 4 hours to 40 minutes"</em>, <em>"stakeholder signed off and became my best reference"</em>.}, q{<strong>规则二：先写结果。</strong>没有结果的故事只是回忆，不是故事。每个结果要带数字或具体后果：<em>"事故从 4 小时缩到 40 分钟"</em>、<em>"利益相关方签了字，后来成了我的推荐人"</em>。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Rule three: Action gets 70% of the airtime.</strong> Most candidates spend 80% of the answer on Situation — weather-reporting the background. The interviewer already knows the background; they came for <em>your verbs</em>. I write Actions as three bullets: what I did, what I said, what I decided.}, q{<strong>规则三：行动占 70% 篇幅。</strong>多数候选人 80% 的时间在讲情境——播报天气预报。面试官不缺背景信息，他们是来听<strong>你的动词</strong>的。我把行动写成三条：做了什么、说了什么、决定了什么。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Rule four: map each story to three questions.</strong> The incident story answers "tell me about a failure" AND "tell me about pressure" AND "tell me about ownership". <em>One story, three doors.</em> Write the mapping on the story card.}, q{<strong>规则四：每个故事映射三个问题。</strong>事故故事可以回答"讲一次失败"，也可以回答"讲一次高压时刻"和"讲一次担当"。<em>一个故事，三扇门。</em>把映射写在故事卡上。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Rule five: end every story with a lesson, in one sentence.</strong> "What I took from that is…" — because the interviewer scores the learning, not just the event. Then say it out loud twice. <em>If it sounds like a slogan, make it smaller and truer.</em>}, q{<strong>规则五：每个故事用一句话的教训收尾。</strong>"我从中学到的是……"——因为面试官打分的是你的成长，而不只是事件。然后大声说两遍。<em>如果听起来像口号，就把它改小、改真。</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{Six stories, results first, actions at 70%, three doors each, one-line lessons. <strong>That is the bank. Now I rehearse transitions, not scripts.</strong>}, q{六个故事、结果先行、行动占七成、每扇门有映射、一句话教训。<strong>这就是故事库。接下来练衔接，不背稿。</strong>}],
],
phrases => [
['Frame', q{Six stories, not twenty.}, q{六个故事，不是二十个。}, q{A small bank you know cold beats a large bank you rehearse badly.}],
['Result', q{Cut from 4 hours to 40 minutes.}, q{从 4 小时缩到 40 分钟。}, q{The before → after number is the backbone of a Result. Time, money, error rate — all work.}],
['Balance', q{Action gets 70% of the airtime.}, q{行动占 70% 的篇幅。}, q{If you cannot fill 70% with verbs, pick a story where you actually did the work.}],
['Flex', q{One story, three doors.}, q{一个故事，三扇门。}, q{Flexing one story to multiple questions is the entire economy of interview prep.}],
['Lesson', q{What I took from that is…}, q{我从中学到的是……}, q{The single sentence that converts an anecdote into evidence of growth.}],
['Reality', q{If it sounds like a slogan, make it smaller and truer.}, q{如果听起来像口号，就改小、改真。}, q{Small true lessons score higher than grand fake ones.}],
