grammar => [
['Past simple carries Actions; past continuous sets the scene', q{<em>"The system was failing every ten minutes. I pulled the logs, I called the vendor, I restarted the queue."</em> The past continuous (was failing) paints the Situation; the string of past simples (pulled, called, restarted) is the Action — short declarative blows, one after another. Action lines should be so clean that each verb could be underlined.}, q{过去进行时（was failing）铺陈情境；一串一般过去时（pulled, called, restarted）构成行动——短促陈述，一击接一击。行动句应该干净到每个动词都能画线强调。}],
['Result tense: the present-perfect echo', q{<em>"Incident cut from 4 hours to 40 minutes — and that framework is still in use today."</em> The Result gets past simple (what changed then) plus an optional present-perfect echo (is still in use) that stretches the value into the interviewer\'s present. One echo sentence per story, no more.}, q{结果用一般过去时（当时改变了什么），可加一句现在完成时的"回声"（is still in use）把价值延伸到面试官的当下。每个故事最多一句回声。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Six is not arbitrary.</strong> Conflict, failure, leadership, pressure, ambiguity, influence — six themes, one story each, and every behavioural question lands on one of them.},
q{<strong>Never memorise sentences, memorise beats.</strong> Scripts break under pressure; beats (S one line, T one line, A three bullets, R one number) survive nerves.},
q{<strong>Use "I", not "we", in Actions.</strong> The interviewer is hiring you. Say "I proposed… I escalated… I wrote…" even inside a team story.},
q{<strong>True numbers only.</strong> Invented metrics collapse under one follow-up question. Approximate honestly: "roughly 40 minutes, down from about 4 hours."},
q{<strong>The same story for failure and success feels honest.</strong> Reusing the incident for "a failure" and "pressure" is not cheating — it is showing one event had many facets.},
],
practice => [
{ t => 'Write one story card', p => 'Pick your best production-incident story. Fill: S (1 sentence), T (1 sentence), A (3 bullets starting with I), R (1 number + 1 echo), Lesson (1 sentence).', a => q{Sanity check: can you tell it in 90 seconds? Is the Result a number or a named consequence? Does the Lesson sound like something a colleague would actually say — not a poster?} },
{ t => 'Map three doors', p => 'Take your story card and list every behavioural question it can legitimately answer. Then mark which two minutes of the story you would emphasise for each door.', a => q{Example: for "pressure", emphasise the 2 AM triage and your comms; for "failure", emphasise the missed monitoring gap and what you changed; for "ownership", emphasise that nobody assigned you the comms role — you took it. Same facts, shifted spotlight.} },
